WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.218
This is the Home screen — the page you land on
every time you open MyWell.

2
00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.626
Let's walk through what each part of it is
telling you.

3
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.730
Now we're on: Home.

4
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:18.114
This is where MyWell opens every day — a hello, your
key numbers, your stations on a map,

5
00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:20.706
and one tap to record a reading.

6
00:00:20.826 --> 00:00:23.682
For this tour you're seeing the world of Asha,

7
00:00:23.802 --> 00:00:28.842
our practice account: a Data Contributor with
a few stations in Badgaon.

8
00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.738
Let's look around.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.830
Your monitoring at a glance.

10
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:38.582
Your two key numbers live here: how many
monitoring stations you have,

11
00:00:38.702 --> 00:00:43.238
and the last measurement you recorded — its
value, when and where.

12
00:00:43.358 --> 00:00:48.518
If that last reading is getting old, it's a
gentle nudge that a field visit is due.

13
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.438
Your stations on a map.

14
00:00:51.558 --> 00:00:54.510
Every pin below is a monitoring station.

15
00:00:54.630 --> 00:01:01.254
Use these two filters to switch between just your stations
and everyone's, or to show a single type only.

16
00:01:01.374 --> 00:01:07.758
Tap any pin to see the station's name, type and
latest reading, and jump to its full record.

17
00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:11.439
Record a reading — the heart of the app.

18
00:01:11.559 --> 00:01:13.935
This is the heart of MyWell.

19
00:01:14.055 --> 00:01:20.295
Tap the picture that matches your water source — a well
for groundwater depth, a rain gauge for rainfall,

20
00:01:20.415 --> 00:01:25.695
a check-dam, river, spring, tank or reservoir
for surface water.

21
00:01:25.815 --> 00:01:30.783
A short form then asks for the value, and you
can attach a photo and notes.

22
00:01:30.903 --> 00:01:37.719
Show all sources reveals every type, including
water-quality readings like pH and TDS.

23
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.326
Shortcuts.

24
00:01:40.446 --> 00:01:46.182
Shortcuts to the common jobs: register a
brand-new station, open the full station map,

25
00:01:46.302 --> 00:01:50.334
or check the weather and rain forecast before
you head to the field.

26
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.926
Recent activity.

27
00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:58.902
Your latest readings collect here, so a typo
or a missed station stands out straight away.

28
00:01:59.022 --> 00:02:02.094
Tap a row to open your full measurement
history.

29
00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:04.861
That is the whole page.

30
00:02:04.981 --> 00:02:09.637
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

31
00:02:09.757 --> 00:02:12.733
Thanks for helping look after our groundwater.
